  "worked_solution": "To transform $A$ into $B,$ we need to make entries to the left and to the right of ${a}_{32}=1$ equal to $0.$\n\nTo do this, we can apply the following elementary column operations:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =[\\begin{aligned}4 & 2 & -9 \\\\ 15 & 4 & -12 \\\\ 3 & 1 & -5\\end{aligned}] &  & \\,\\begin{aligned}{C}_{1}:={C}_{1}-3{C}_{2}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & \u223c[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 2 & -9 \\\\ 3 & 4 & -12 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -5\\end{aligned}] &  & \\,\\begin{aligned}{C}_{3}:={C}_{3}+5{C}_{2}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & \u223c[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 3 & 4 & 8 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =B\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the elementary column operations are\n\n$\\,$ ${C}_{1}:={C}_{1}-3{C}_{2}\\,$ and $\\,{C}_{3}:={C}_{3}+5{C}_{2}.$",
